WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.600
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.980
Being together like this...

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.900
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.310
Forever...

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.830
...under this sky...

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.440
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.130
In this beauty...

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.240
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.290
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.420
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.010
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.080
...and more loving...

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.170
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.390
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.690
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.080
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.760
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.940
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.640
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.740
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.390
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.520
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.600
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.460
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.830
If you go there...

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.830
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.210
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.690
Under this sky...

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.340
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.060
Being together like this...

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.590
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.780
Under this sky...

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.270
...we'll walk together!

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.800
Having received a request from the famous
elite school, Shibusawa Academy,

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.640
Meg and Ryuu go undercover to investigate.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:45.180
But soon after they do, the best student
in the school, Kogure Junya, is kidnapped

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:47.940
and his murder broadcast over the net.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:56.110
And that night, Asabuki Maya, who had been investigating
with them, was attacked on a live broadcast!

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:02.410
Ryuu figured out the criminals alibi from
a video recorded at the time of the crime

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.950
and then brought all the students
connected to the crime together

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.290
to show them videos from the time when they
were all in the same middle school movie club.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.550
And from their statements there, he
found out who the criminal was.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.800
in the first crime remained a mystery.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.760
I couldn't just sit on the sidelines any more

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:28.640
so I went to join them, and found a line
of ants heading into the crime scene.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:31.610
I see... that's how!

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.280
Kogure Junya with this.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:41.820
Excuse me.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.790
What? You guys are still standing there?

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.700
Excuse me, please let us check the inside.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:51.580
No way. I told you, civilians aren't allowed

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.880
I'm Amakusa Ryuu from DDS.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:57.630
DDS?

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.720
No wonder you didn't seem like a normal student.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.220
You're with DDS?

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:09.600
Here it is.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.350
Yeah!

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:11.690
There's a bunch of ants!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:19.360
Detective, send this to forensics and
have them analyze it right away.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.320
There's no doubt about it.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:28.700
The criminal used an alibi trick in the first crime too.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.750
The fog's cleared.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:35.630
Then let's get all the suspects together, and...

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.630
No, we don't have enough definitive proof yet.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:43.720
I get it...

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.770
The criminal was extremely careful during the first crime.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:55.650
But when he attacked Asabuki-san, it was
a sudden thing, so he made a mistake.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.520
A mistake?

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:57.730
Yeah.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.490
We're just about to go and make sure of that.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.490
What's wrong?

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:10.700
Somebody dug that flower out.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:20.670
What's this video?

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.840
The video recorded right before Asabuki-san was attacked.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:33.100
This Is it.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.320
What's the counter's time say?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.940
Umm... 30:12.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.400
There's no doubt about it.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.490
Ryuu, we can't just sit here.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:51.040
If we don't hurry they might come after your life!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.160
Life?

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:55.210
Let's try it.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:05.930
To: All concerned parties
I've discovered the identity of the “collector”.
Please head to the meeting room now
Amakusa Ryuu

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.860
Amakusa-kun, you said you had
found the criminal, is this true?

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.150
But, why did you call us all here?

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:26.820
I'm sorry to make you all come here

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:31.790
You see, the real criminal is one of you.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:33.290
What?

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.800
Well, let's drink some coffee and talk about it.

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:47.180
I knew it, he's figured out everything

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.510
I need to shut him up somehow.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:53.810
Here you go, Ryuu-kun.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:55.140
Thanks.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.400
Yes?

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.610
It's Amakusa.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.440
Now's my chance.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:05.440
Sorry for the wait

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.750
Now, drink up.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.920
That'll finish everything.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.250
Excuse me.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:25.510
What?

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.510
We're here to fix this room's air conditioner...

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.720
Now?

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.350
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.100
Can't be helped.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.560
OK then, let's go to the next room.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.600
I'll carry your drinks.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.110
What?

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.400
I'll bring this to the other room.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.030
W-What?

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:48.700
This isn't good.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.870
I'll leave it here.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.620
Umm, we can just give the coffee out at random, right?

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.250
It doesn't look like anybody's drunk it.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:03.210
I can't tell which cup has the poison in it...

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.760
Drink up.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:10.970
There's a 1 in 7 chance...

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.930
It's good.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.220
That's not it.

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:17.140
Everybody, drink up.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.980
Who... who has it?

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.370
They're all fine?

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.580
That means...

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.040
It's either mine...

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.750
Or Amakusa's..

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:44.630
Which is it?

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.130
Which cup has the poison?

00:07:58.500 --> 00:07:59.600
What's wrong?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.230
You aren't going to drink your coffee?

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:10.530
All of you just proved your innocence by drinking
that coffee without any hesitation.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.620
What kind of nonsense?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:24.330
The reason you haven't drunk your coffee is because
it contains the wolfsbane that you put in it.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:25.920
Wolfsbane?

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.960
I'm sure some of you know this already,

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:31.670
but the root of wolfsbane contains deadly poison.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.430
One plant was taken out of the school's flower beds,

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:38.850
so we thought that there might
be another murder planned.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.350
So we thought we'd give you a push,

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.480
and you did just what we thought.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.690
So then we come.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:53.650
We're actually students at DDS.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:54.820
Nice

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.080
DDS, that's...

00:08:58.430 --> 00:08:59.450
that famous-

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:02.250
So are Ryuu and Meg.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:06.670
I used my photographic memory to
tell which cup had the poison in it,

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.210
and made sure that he got it.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.510
Then you knew who did it?

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:18.720
And we knew that the criminal
was panicked by my actions.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:22.640
So we decided to put on a little play.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:27.860
If you hadn't done anything, we
wouldn't have had any proof.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.110
You can't get out of this one.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.110
The murderer of Kogure Junya and
Asabuki Maya, the “collector”, is...

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:36.870
YOU!

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.840
The murderer of Kogure Junya and
Asabuki Maya, the “collector”, is...

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:46.920
YOU!

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:53.510
Tominaga Masashi.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.270
You're the "collector".

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.440
Tominaga-kun is.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.060
Just with that?

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:08.780
My stomach hurts today, and
don't feel like drinking coffee.

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:10.570
What are you saying?

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:14.080
I was with you when Kogure was killed

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:21.040
and anybody could've done the
alibi trick used with Asabuki.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.130
Where's your proof it was me?

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:27.630
You've already given that proof yourself.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:29.800
This is how it happened.

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:34.050
Asabuki-san set her clock for 9 that night.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:38.520
But because the criminal advanced the clock,

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:44.360
she pressed the record button earlier than she
wanted to, and the quiz show was recorded.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:52.200
But, I didn't know how much
the clock had been advanced.

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:53.780
What?

00:10:54.010 --> 00:11:00.160
Even then, afterwards, when I gathered everyone and 
showed them the tapes from when
they were in middle school,

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.710
you were so worried about whether you'd given any
identify you as the criminal

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.380
that you slipped and said something
that only the criminal would know.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:17.260
Yeah, to think that the clock on the
video was advanced by 30 minutes.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:23.230
I was able to determing that, just like you said,
the clock was advanced by 30 minutes

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:25.520
for the first time just a short while ago.

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:32.860
Then, Amakusa, how do you explain the fact
that I was with you when Kogure was killed?

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:37.580
We could see the clock tower
in the window on that video.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:40.450
And its time was 5:15.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.830
At that time I was looking for Minami with you!

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:50.130
It's true that you were with Amakusa-kun that whole time.

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:56.680
couldn't have advanced
that clock like wth Asabuki.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.770
The clock tower's securely locked.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:04.640
Unfortunately, that alibi is gone too.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:05.980
What?

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:12.940
Tominaga-kun, you managed that Alibi
trick by killing Kogure Junya twice.

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:15.370
Twice?

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:16.490
Yes.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:22.410
The hint is that one day space between
Kogure's disappearance and his death.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:28.080
Actually, the 5:15 we saw on the footage over
the net, wasn't on the day he was killed.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.920
It was the day earlier.

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:40.930
In order to get your alibi, you made a fake
snuff video on the day before the crime.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:49.480
And the next day, using Meg as a
witness, you killed him for real

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:58.820
and then edited the two videos
to make them look like one.

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:00.780
Wait.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:05.580
The criminal hit Kogure's head with that bottle hard.

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:12.960
That he had no wounds whatsoever the next
day, when we saw him, which is impossible.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:17.340
Then let's give it a try!

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:24.850
What are you doing?

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:32.020
He's fine?

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.530
Here, lick it.

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:40.820
It's sweet.

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:45.540
Yeah, you see this on TV shows and

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:47.540
a candy beer bottle.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:48.330
Candy?

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:56.010
It seems that, when you hit somebody during a movie,
use a candy beer bottle so it won't hurt them.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:02.600
That's what he used in his fake snuff video,

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:18.320
and afterwards, while he thought he'd cleaned
carefully, small pieces were still left on the floor.

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:24.280
The line of ants I saw was carrying that candy beer bottle.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:32.040
I remember now. Didn't your dad let us see a movie
set when we were in middle school, Tominaga-kun?

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:37.630
That day they were recording a scene where
somebody got hit with a beer bottle,

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:42.970
And it was Asabuki who was doing the taping.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:47.020
The master tape of that was still at her house.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:53.610
The video #7 that was taken from
her room was a copy of that.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:15:00.700
He probably went to her room as she had seen
that at the time she called me about it.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:04.700
Actually, now that you mention it, it's
a middle school movie of Kogure.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:06.950
The same middle school as me.

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:12.670
The others were Oobayashi, Touya, and Tominaga.
also were in the same middle school. And actually...

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:16.800
Ah, it seems like someone came. I'll call you back.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:17.920
Coming!

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:24.090
Oh, it's just Tominaga, come in!

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:27.930
I was just watching a video from our movie club.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:32.020
I thought Ryuu might learn something
if we showed it to him.

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:41.070
If I had had seen this tape,
it may have given me a hint to break your alibi.

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:46.660
So you attacked Asabuki-san to take her tape.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:50.370
Tominaga Masashi, admit your guilt.

00:15:58.110 --> 00:16:00.710
Why? Weren't you all friends?

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.260
How could you

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:08.560
Friends... I didn't have any friends.

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:16.350
I had plenty who pretended to be
my friends, but no real friends.

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:20.570
Except for one, Ogura Emina.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:22.740
Ogura Emina?

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:24.240
What?

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:27.070
We had been had been dating.

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:29.700
No way. When did that start?

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:34.710
Dating at a dorm school like this;
everybody'd find out right away.

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.580
No you wouldn't.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:40.960
We'd only been dating over the net.

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:50.720
I fell in love with a girl named "Anime" on a
movie-lover's web page that the school ran.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.680
And one day, I noticed...

00:16:56.790 --> 00:17:00.440
If you read this backwards it becomes Emina.

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:02.730
It's Ogura Emina.

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:04.610
I was happy.

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:08.700
I'd liked her since middle school.

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:15.910
What's this?

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:29.680
I tried my best to make them stop, but it kept going.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.220
And, at last...

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.850
Emina left what seemed like her last words,

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:42.020
and vanished from the school and from the net.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:47.280
I frantically searched for the identity of
the person who'd done this to her...

00:17:48.680 --> 00:17:49.450
and...

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:51.280
at last, I found it.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:58.330
They were all Kogure Junya's comments.

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:03.250
Dammit. I hate that girl.

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:07.880
Emina for having better grades than

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:14.180
I couldn't forgive him for driving Emina to kill herself.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:16.770
So I...

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:17.980
Wait!

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:24.020
Umm...

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:26.570
I have something

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:29.110
to say about that.

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:37.040
I don't know why Ogura-san vanished,

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:43.790
but I know it wasn't because of Kogure's bullying.

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.130
What do you know?

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:50.510
You don't have any friends, let alone a boyfriend.

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:55.010
Listen, Emina and I really understood each other.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:56.600
She—

00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:57.560
You're
wrong!

00:18:58.250 --> 00:18:58.850
No way!

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:00.940
Touya-san.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:02.520
That's not it.

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:05.110
Anime wasn't Ogura Emina.

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:08.570
It was me!

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:19.790
Just like you, I always admired her.

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:24.250
She was so pretty, cheerful, and she had so many friends.

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.960
I wanted to be like her.

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:32.260
So then I though. I could be her on the net.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:37.890
And so I changed my handle to a 
variation of her name: "Anime".

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:45.400
And eventually, I got to be friends with somebody
named ‘Spielberg’, and I was so happy!

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:46.360
You're lying!

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:49.940
Why you...

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:51.950
You're lying, bitch!

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:52.700
Hold it!

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:54.030
Touya-san!

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:57.620
It's True!

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:03.830
You told me your dreams for the future
in that chat room with only the two of us in it.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:10.710
You said you wanted to make a great movie,
with a good script, really good actors

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:14.550
and without any expensive special effects.

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:16.510
You're...

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.390
Are you really Anime?

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:24.770
But all those people were saying horrible things about me,

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:29.070
so I decided to “kill myself" by stopping posting.

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:33.520
And then, Ogura-san really vanished!

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:34.420
No Way.

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:40.490
Then the motive for this case was
a misunderstanding on the net?

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:41.040
I

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:45.620
What?

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:49.540
So I vowed my revenge over nothing?

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:52.340
I was an idiot... such an idiot.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:06.980
Hey, stop it!

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:09.310
Let me go!

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:13.320
Let me go!

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:38.390
Yes?

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:40.720
Asabuki!

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.640
You're alive!

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:43.850
Yeah.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:49.350
If he knew she was alive she might've
been attacked again, so...

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:53.570
we didn't tell everybody that she'd survived.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.490
I see.

00:21:55.930 --> 00:21:57.490
You're really amazing, Ryuu-kun.

00:21:57.890 --> 00:21:59.610
It's too bad you're leaving.

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:01.660
Where's Touya?

00:22:02.350 --> 00:22:05.410
She was more shocked than anybody by this.

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:07.830
She said she'd be going back to her home for a while.

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:10.330
That's?

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:13.960
Videos from our movie club.

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:17.630
Everybody looks like friends.

00:22:18.990 --> 00:22:23.140
I knew that Tominaga's parents had divorced
and that a lot of other stuff had happened,

00:22:23.950 --> 00:22:25.220
but he acted fine.

00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:27.930
We all pretended like we didn't care.

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:33.730
Just like he said, we can't say we were really friends.

00:22:39.180 --> 00:22:42.990
Minami-kun, Amakusa-kun, you did very well this time.

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:45.200
Thank you, sir.

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:50.120
Dan-sensei, what happened to the student
who vanished, Ogura Emina?

00:22:51.400 --> 00:22:54.710
That was actually settled in a very surprising manner.

00:22:55.030 --> 00:22:58.210
Actually, we got a message from her herself.

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:04.470
It seems she'd eloped with a lover
who her parents opposed,

00:23:05.450 --> 00:23:10.190
but she read about this incident in the
papers, and contacted the school.

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:15.730
Then I feel really bad for Tominaga, somehow.

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:23.700
Yeah.

00:23:24.470 --> 00:23:27.120
But... he's better, maybe...

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:32.170
than somebody who was born to be a murderer.

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:34.210
Ryuu-kun?

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.420
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:49.760
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:52.430
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.090
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.090 --> 00:23:56.100
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.390
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.390 --> 00:24:00.930
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:02.730
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.980
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:10.610
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:13.700
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:16.120
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.240
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:19.790
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.460
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.670
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:26.880
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:30.380
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:33.340
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:35.260
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:37.640
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:40.470
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:42.450 --> 00:24:46.310
Right after this!

00:24:48.080 --> 00:24:49.810
Beautiful flowers bloom at DDS!

00:24:50.250 --> 00:24:51.400
Minami Megumi,

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:56.440
Preview

00:24:51.420 --> 00:24:52.690
Yukihira Sakurako

00:24:52.710 --> 00:24:55.440
and the mysterious girl who joins the A-Class!

00:24:56.090 --> 00:24:59.030
The beautiful detective group, "Trio Da Beauty", is created!

00:24:57.470 --> 00:25:06.410
Right after this. don't give up Kazuma!

00:24:59.760 --> 00:25:02.030
Placing themselves in danger to find the criminal,

00:25:02.470 --> 00:25:04.870
they combine forces and capture the enemy
of beautiful women everywhere!

00:25:05.350 --> 00:25:06.660
There's one answer!

00:25:12.190 --> 00:25:13.210
What?

00:25:14.820 --> 00:25:19.090
I was just thinking that we really don't
make convincing looking janitors.
